00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:08.195
LILIANA YU: Peter Bakkum, the
platform lead at Quizlet Inc.

00:00:08.195 --> 00:00:11.840
said, "We believe GCP has
better core technology,

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.560
in particular, its networking
and disk technology."

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.430
Thanks, Peter.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.320
We really appreciate that.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.310
A huge component of why that may
be is Google's persistent disk.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.400
Persistent disks are durable
network storage devices

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.460
that your instances can
access, like physical disks

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.590
in a desktop or a server.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.290
The data on each persistent
disk is distributed

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.750
across several physical disks.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.260
Compute Engine manages the
physical disks and the data

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.350
distribution to ensure
redundancy and optimize

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.210
performance for you.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.510
Persistent disk offers
multi-reader capability.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.240
With multi-reader mounting,
many virtual machines

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.880
can read data from a
single persistent disk

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.070
with no performance degradation.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.300
Multi-reader mounting makes
sharing content a snap.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.820
This lab will take you about
30 minutes to complete,

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.250
and you'll learn how to create
a virtual machine instance,

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.990
create a new persistent
disk, attach persistent disks

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:11.830
to a virtual machine
instance, format

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:14.960
and mount the persistent
disk, and automatically mount

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.660
the disk on restart.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.060
Persistent disks are
located independently

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.040
from your virtual
machine instances.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.680
So you can detach or
remove persistent disks

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.970
to keep your data even after
you delete your instances.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:32.210
This is the fifth lab in
the GCP Essentials Quest.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.610
Completing this quest
earns you this badge

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.590
to recognize your achievement.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.620
Next up, Hello Node Kubernetes.

